---
name: odbcpp-development-batch
description: Prepare, qualify, review and integrate a bounded ODBCPP implementation batch, including parallel ownership and evidence handoff. Use for project development or continuation; ordinary explanatory questions do not require the batch workflow.
---

# ODBCPP development batch

Use `AGENTS.md` for repository rules and the active handoff for current facts.
Apply its build storage and periodic cleanup policy before resource admission and
at batch closure; the coordinator owns integration, shared resources and cleanup.
Apply `PARALLEL_WORKFLOW.md` for the human-approved continuous four-owner execution model and
separate source, resource and integration/live migration releases. The 12-hour cadence and protected acceptance stay unchanged.
Do not turn this workflow into new product scope or execution permission.

## Apply the 2026-10-13 local reset

Use the current local development reset in `PARALLEL_WORKFLOW.md` ahead of old
lane briefs/private controller admissions. `odbcpp-1` alone directs AO workers;
an outside maintenance reset uses an explicit coordinator handoff. A root-assigned
exclusive policy lease permits worker authorship without creating a second coordinator. Resume reviewed feature implementation and ordinary owned
CMake/CTest qualification under the existing common slot. Do not make pristine
pre-code execution, generated-source category approval, full compiler/loader
provenance or bespoke guardian/controller proof a routine local prerequisite.
Record actual HEAD/diff/configuration/dependency/binary/tests/results and finite
command supervision/cleanup; keep measured disk reserve and architecture checks.
Preserve every historical STOP/failure, use fresh development graphs, and review
one complete candidate/evidence package. The reset grants no cloud/live/private
PostgreSQL authority or relaxation of protected final acceptance.

## Select and isolate

Read the actual Git state, applicable plans and current task evidence. Name the
contract gap and observable completion condition before selecting files. Check
the current Redshift product task, work board and actual agents. After the
coordinator records `source_lanes_released=true` from the existing owner's scope/
lease acknowledgment, dispatch four dependency-compatible complete product packages under exact leases. Package
owners implement and investigate automated focused qualification; independent
reviewers are drawn from a shared pool when candidates are ready. Do not create
permanent three-agent sets, per-lane app goals or timers. Setup can proceed now,
and released source lanes can implement in isolation while the existing immutable
live checkpoint remains owned. Product builds require `heavy_builds_released=true`
from resource release; integration/live transfer requires the owner's terminal,
reaps, principal cleanup and accounting release (`integration_live_released=true`).
Pending live acceptance is not a blanket blocker for isolated source packages.

For independent implementation, inspect attached managed worktrees first.
Preserve dirty historical checkouts. Create a new managed worktree at the exact
selected integration commit if no suitable checkout exists; explicitly select
`codex/transport-foundation` and pin its exact head rather than using a tool's
remote-default branch. Use the returned directory, not
the integration checkout. A read-only audit can use existing immutable evidence.
Do not relocate a running build or silently replace an accepted scratch path.

Before implementation, classify shared SDK foundations, backend-specific work
and adapter-only behavior under `SDK_ARCHITECTURE.md` and the ownership checkpoint
in `AGENTS.md`. Carry the component/file/rationale/dependency/proof table into the
candidate handoff and require independent final review of actual placement.
Reuse the existing architecture checks; do not create a standalone test batch
for a prose-only policy update or defer common ownership without a disposition.

Every delegated assignment states baseline, owned files, permitted actions,
deliverable, required checks and stop condition. Record leased contracts and
interface dependencies before concurrent work. A bounded lease can include
SDK/CMake/CI/crypto/ODBC files; serialize overlapping leases and prerequisite
contract changes. Workers may commit/push their assigned branches and open PRs;
the coordinator alone changes the integration branch and integrates reviewed bytes.
Return an exact patch and evidence rather than restoring an old whole CMake,
manifest or plan file over current work.

## Implement and verify

Preserve behavior outside the selected contract. Keep existing test assertions;
repair a faulty fixture only with a source-backed explanation and retained first
failure. Choose checks that test observable behavior or a meaningful boundary.
Low-impact prose changes need review, not a repeated full product build.
Every new or changed `if`, `else`, `for` or `while` body containing GoogleTest
macros must use explicit braces, including enclosing nested assertion controls.
Keep control statements and assertion-containing bodies on readable separate
lines. Before expensive builds and during candidate review, run the cheap
changed-source check against the exact batch base:

```sh
python3 -B tools/development/check_changed_gtest_control_flow.py --base <exact-batch-base> <changed-C++-paths>
# For an immutable candidate review, also pass --head <exact-candidate-head>.
python3 -B tools/development/test_changed_gtest_control_flow.py
```

The checker uses full-file lexical context while selecting only changed code;
it ignores unrelated historical blocks, comments and literal contents. An
unsupported changed scope requires explicit manual review, never a guessed
pass. This authoring/review check is not compiler or GCC proof, a new full-graph
gate or permission to change compiler warnings. Preserve assertion conditions,
macro arguments, test names and original diagnostics when repairing fixtures.
Owners 2/3 use `tools/development/with_build_slot.py` for one heavy configure/build/regression
slot on this 8 GiB host. Keep an owned build directory and durable retention reason.
Do not bypass the legacy resource-release fence, run duplicate heavy builds or replay a
passed gate just because another lane has completed.

Record actual source/configuration/executable identity, selected test inventory,
exit status and qualification limits. Source checks and mocked controls do not
prove compiler, provider, TLS or live behavior. A proposal is not implementation.
Do not label a test passed before its process completes and results are read.

Owner 4 uses the default-off normal Ubuntu product mode in `PARALLEL_WORKFLOW.md`,
not a local heavy graph or another benchmark. The coordinator automatically
manually dispatches reviewed immutable workflow W and separate product P: one
standard free Ubuntu 24.04 x64 job, j2/30 minutes, one global noncancelling remote
heavy group. Run the changed-diff brace check before expensive commands. Use
literal allowlisted owning GoogleTest targets, six architecture checks and 23 SDK
headers with the existing REDSHIFT Release/GCC/unixODBC SQLWCHAR2/OpenSSL shared
profile. Configure fresh, restore only an exact compatible owning producer's
compiler objects after independent compiler/dependency/full-flags/profile/path/
ccache checks, and link/test fresh. No fallback keys, binaries or graphs. Cache is
at most 256 MiB; source-only evidence is at most 20 MiB/job with three-day retention.
Retain P/W before/after, source/config/dependency/object/executable/XML/inventory/
run-attempt and failure/phase evidence. Maximum child RSS is not aggregate peak;
missing provider step precision stays explicit. Linux proof leaves macOS/full/
platform/native/live/final debt. No paid/secrets/services/privatePG authority.

Owner 5 uses the separate default-off Windows owning job in `PARALLEL_WORKFLOW.md`
under sole coordinator dispatch after independent workflow/safety review. Inspect
actual x64 MSVC/Visual Studio multiconfig POSTGRESQL Release/Windows ODBC2/OpenSSL
BUNDLED_SHARED configuration. Live/TLS probes are OFF. First job is cold: no cache,
restored binaries or graph. Build real owning GoogleTests, new core/driver links
and SDK23, run six applicable architecture checks, and retain source/configuration,
actual compiler argv/response/dependency tlogs, objects/libs/DLL/exe hashes and
complete inventory/XML. One free public Windows 2025 j2/30-minute global
noncancelling job may overlap the separate Ubuntu slot; local capacity is unchanged.
Text evidence is <=20 MiB/three days, direct-process peak is not aggregate peak.
No services/registry/MSI/native SQL/paid/secrets/cloud/privatePG authority. Preserve
first failures and obtain a narrow root code lease for findings. The owner continues
substantial source packages after proof; setup does not establish adoption or add
a feature count. Product approval may be reused only unchanged; Windows results
and current integration applicability require independent assessment.

## Review and integrate

Have a finite independent review assess actual candidate bytes and evidence.
Resolve concrete findings in a separate preserved successor; do not rerun an
unchanged accepted package for reassurance. Before applying, verify current
baseline, pins, exact selected diff, apply/reverse checks and unrelated changes.

For Redshift, apply [DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md](../../../DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md).
Owners 2/3 use macOS/iODBC UCS4 as the primary local development profile: focused checks, then
relevant coherent regression/staging/architecture/package checks. Collect additional width/sanitizer/platform/provider
checks into the 12-hour sweep; run one early only for actual failure, immediate
safety/ABI diagnosis, or explicit human request, with a
recorded reason. Do not claim unexecuted profiles passed. Keep independent review,
source/binary binding, bounded execution and PostgreSQL/process cleanup.

Reviewed primary-qualified commits and pushes continue with full-CI/live
acceptance pending. Author live GoogleTests with the feature and queue their
execution; do not create per-feature paid admission. The coordinator uses the
existing private ci-cadence.json for a combined checkpoint every 12 hours without
resuming the paused continuation:
first make full GitHub CI green on the exact ready pushed head, then run the
accumulated new/affected and applicable authorized Redshift regression cases in
one reviewed finite live batch. Group failures into coherent reviewed fixes,
push, restore exact-head green full CI before corrected live execution and rerun
only affected cases under fresh admission. Reuse validated runners and accepted
unchanged evidence; use one combined admission review and one result/final review.
Do not duplicate watchers, repeatedly rebuild admission scaffolding or stop ready
product implementation for pending periodic acceptance. Existing goals remain unfinished until their original acceptance is actually
proved. Future implementation goals use the measurable implementation/primary/
review/commit-push/debt-recording scope in DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md; their closure
does not close pending platform/live qualification. Scheduled acceptance is not an
implementation blocker for the next authorized product package.

Group related actual failures into reviewed corrections and re-run affected gates;
retain unchanged evidence only by actual source/input applicability. Do not replay
native tests for compiler-only repairs. Live/native work still requires existing
finite authority; this cadence grants none. Existing full-acceptance goals and final release acceptance still
require the full required graph (PostgreSQL/Unicode/TLS/Redshift/sanitizer/offline,
SDK/architecture/package and platform/provider CI), exact-head green full CI,
independent final audit and verified shutdown/reaps. A primary green is insufficient for full acceptance.

A completed failed full CI may be followed by a bounded reviewed repair after its
watcher is reaped and original evidence retained. Follow one successor full run;
do not weaken tests or mix unrelated source into a claimed repair-only candidate.

## Close the finite package

Report what changed, why, actual checks and remaining limits. Mark only the
finite package complete; synthetic milestones do not close native acquisition
and verified login. Return the concise candidate handoff specified in
`PARALLEL_WORKFLOW.md`; report worker completion separately from accepted integration. The coordinator updates
current handoff/work-board facts in place and selects or continues the next
ready authorized product package after applicable source-lane release. Preserve archived
failures and protected cloud admission. Keep secrets and credential/accounting artifacts outside the repo.

The coordinator's existing authorized implementation goals chain immediately after
verified integration closure; the existing timer complements execution and runs
accumulated acceptance. Work-board entries track lanes without per-lane app goals
or timers. Keep legacy 15-minute continuation PAUSED, cost monitor 12-hour ACTIVE
and existing human 5-minute supervision; no automatic resume. Each continuing
owner has an exact assignment, a named wait with owner and resumption event/deadline,
or promptly reported genuine human decision. Closure immediately resumes the next
root-selected authorized package; neither six packages nor pilot closure ends the
mission. Reuse/rename the stable session for its current package and verify names.
Preserve full-CI/live/final debt in continuation/acceptance-backlog.json before
closing any implementation goal. Existing full-acceptance app objectives require
supported redefinition or actual full closure; never mark them complete by prose
reinterpretation. Neither is test evidence or paid-action authority. Side chats are
useful for user explanations; the main development chat retains integration
ownership. Inline diff comments and independent review assess concrete changes.

## Batch size and diagnostic execution

The human-approved 2026-10-11 trial above supersedes the older per-batch full
CI sequencing in this 2026-10-07 agreement; live controls are unchanged.

Default to coherent workflow batches, normally three to five related scenarios
when ready and compatible, rather than a separate integration cycle per case.
Run focused checks while developing, then relevant coherent primary regression
and independent integration review. Intermediate pushes may precede the periodic
full graph and full CI under DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md; full final acceptance stays
mandatory.
Preserve each scenario's assertions and result; never add unrelated work merely
to fill a batch or replay already qualified milestones.

CI and real Redshift tests provide distinct evidence. Under the human-approved
12-hour policy, first make full GitHub CI green on the exact tested head, then
execute the accumulated live batch. Earlier diagnostic live execution requires
explicit human scheduling direction and unchanged finite authority/admission;
ordinary feature completion is not an exception. Preserve original failures,
source/binary binding, independent review and exact-principal cleanup.

Group ready, reviewed live scenarios into one finite cluster session with explicit
per-case and aggregate statement/time bounds, durable one-use admission and
verified exact-principal cleanup and pause. Keep the cluster paused during gaps
in its admitted test session, including coding/builds/CI needed for that session;
do not keep it running to await speculative readiness. A genuinely executing
bounded live batch may overlap acknowledged isolated source lanes. Spending,
resource, principal, network and authorization horizons are unchanged.
